data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Mission m1 summary: greet, tested — campaign-met\\n\\n## Mission criteria (mission.md)\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — **satisfied**\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — **satisfied**\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — **satisfied**\\n\\n## How the campaign ran\\n- Recorded plan (`note plan`), then dispatched the full task to dev (d002).\\n- dev replied claiming completion (commit `ece8bfe` on\\n  `cs-sandbox/dev-97a3d923.csrocfw-97a3d923` — actual branch:\\n  `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`).\\n- Judged by evidence, not by the report: fetched dev's branch, read both files\\n  from the branch, checked out a detached worktree, and ran the verification\\n  command myself — 2 tests ran, OK, exit code 0.\\n- Accepted dev's d002; recorded assessment (`note assessment`).\\n\\n## Verified deliverables (on dev's branch, head `ece8bfe`)\\n- `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"` — exact spec,\\n  including the empty-string edge case (`greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: `unittest` module with `test_normal_name`\\n  (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`); imports `greet` via `sys.path` insertion of\\n  `\u003croot\u003e/src`, so discovery from the repo root works.\\n- Verification re-run by me from a clean checkout: `python3 -m unittest\\n  discover -s tests` -\u003e exit 0.\\n\\n## Outcome\\nEvery stated criterion is satisfied — **campaign-met**. Nothing remains unmet.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/m1-summary.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_35","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461740,"id":"chatcmpl-389101d82a834cbf960513cb2dff5e5b","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

